If the chosen isolated composite is the system plus all relevant surroundings, then

The process is internally reversible when \(S_{\mathrm{gen}}=0\) and irreversible when \(S_{\mathrm{gen}}>0\). A nonisolated system can have \(\Delta S<0\) by exporting enough entropy with heat, so the unqualified statement \(\Delta S\geq0\) is false for a general system.

Working:
Begin from the preceding result
\[
\Delta S_{\mathrm{univ}}
=\Delta S_{\mathrm{system}}+\Delta S_{\mathrm{surroundings}}
